details:
(a) the total number of Union Government Ministries, Departments and Bodies onboarded on the SHe-Box portal till date;
(b) the number of Government Ministries/Departments onboarded on the portal that have updated their Internal Complaint Committee details; and
(c) Ministries and Departments under the Union Government that have not been onboarded on the portal and the details thereof?

(a) the number of complaints registered on the Ayush Suraksha portal since its inception, year-wise and category wise;
(b) the number of complaints disposed and pending till date and the details thereof; and
(c) whether any repeat offenders have been identified based on the complaints, if so, the details of such offenders and the action taken against them?

(a) the targeted expenditure as the percentage of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) under the New Education Policy;
(b) the expenditure on education as percentage of GDP as of 1st January, 2026; and
(c) Union Government`s share in the total expenditure on education?

(a) the details of number of times extensions provided to the Smart City Mission (SCM) since inception;
(b) whether there exists any definition of Smart Cities, if so the details thereof; and
(c) whether it is a fact that as of 1st February, 2026 only 31cities has been transformed as Smart city?

(a) the statutory and administrative architecture governing the SHe-Box (Sexual Harassment electronic Box) Portal and the institutional mechanisms through which complaints are received, processed and escalated;
(b) the total number of complaints received on the Portal during the last five years, year-wise; and
(c) the number of complaints disposed of, pending and under various stages of inquiry, along with the average and median time taken for disposal?

(a) the total number of Farmer Produce Organizations (FPOs) in country as on 1st January, 2026;
(b) the total number of FPOs that have been registered as 100 percent women members; and
(c) the total number of women farmers out of the overall registration in all FPOs in the country?

(a) the number of judges per ten lakh of population in the country, separately for the Supreme court, High Courts and Lower Judiciary, State-wise;
(b) the number of judges per ten lakh as suggested by the Supreme Court;
(c) the country-wise details of judges per ten lakh population; and
(d) the details of top ten countries with highest judges to population ratio?

(a) the number of sanctioned posts, in position and the number of vacancies, including reserved posts across categories in the Ministry of Home Affairs;
(b) the details of the number of vacancies in the Ministry and Department, including reserved posts since 2021, year-wise and category-wise; and
(c) the details of the number of contractual employees hired since 2021, year-wise and category-wise?

(a) the number of sanctioned posts, in position and the number of vacancies, including reserved posts across categories in the Ministry;
(b) the number of vacancies in the Ministry, including reserved posts since 2020-21, year-wise and category-wise; and
(c) the number of contractual employees hired since 2020-21, year-wise and category-wise?

(a) the country-wise and year-wise details of total amount of tea (in kg) imported since 2020;
(b) whether India imports duty-free tea from any country, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of import duty imposed by the countries on tea that is imported from India;
(d) whether it is a fact that import of tea is permitted only for the purpose of re-export; and
(e) whether Government has any data on imported tea being mixed with domestic produce?

(a) the number of sanctioned posts and the number of vacancies, including reserved posts across categories in the Ministry;
(b) the number of vacancies in the Ministry and its subordinate offices, including reserved posts since 2020, year-wise and category-wise; and
(c) the number of contractual employees hired since then, year-wise and category-wise?

(a) whether Government has compiled the data on coastal erosion;
(b) if so, the details thereof including the percentage of total coastline vulnerable to erosion; and
(c) the year-wise details of budgetary allocation made for the National Coastal Mission during the last five years?

(a) the rank-wise total sanctioned strength and vacancies under Delhi Police;
(b) the duration for which these posts have remained vacant; and
(c) timeline for filling these vacancies?

(a) the sanctioned strength and actual number of Doctors and Specialists working in all Central Government Hospitals, Hospital-wise;
(b) the sanctioned strength and actual number of Nurses, Paramedical and other Support Staff in all Central Government Hospitals, Hospital-wise; and
(c) the proposed timeline for filling these vacancies?

(a) the details of total loans disbursed by National, Private and Cooperative banks to the farmers during last five years, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) the details of total loans disbursed by National, Private and Cooperative banks to the students during last five years, State-wise and year-wise;
(c) the details of total loans disbursed by National, Private and Cooperative banks to the MSME during last five years, State-wise, and year-wise; and
(d) the details of total loans disbursed by National, Private and Cooperative banks to the Corporates during last five years, State-wise and year-wise?

(a) details of the number and percentage of households that remain unelectrified in rural and urban areas, area-wise;
(b) the number and percentage of unelectrified households belonging to economically weaker sections;
(c) whether it is a fact that the current definition of an “electrified village” requires only 10 per cent of the households in that village to have electricity; and
(d) if so, whether Government plans to revise this definition?

(a) whether Government of India has taken any steps for the formation of an Indo-Bhutan Joint River Commission to address the issues related to trans-boundary rivers between India and Bhutan;
(b) if so, the present status of the proposal for constituting such a Commission; and
(c) whether Government is aware of the recurring problems of floods, erosion and siltation caused by rivers originating in Bhutan and flowing into the Indian territory, particularly in the border districts of Alipurduar and Jalpaiguri?

(a) whether Government has any data on percentage of total population dependent on agriculture;
(b) if so, the details thereof as of 30th November 2025; and
(c) the details of budgetary allocations to the Department of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare’s, their percentage share of the total Central Plan outlay for the last three years, and year-wise utilisation?

(a) whether it is a fact that the pending dues under the MGNREGS scheme amounts to more than one-fourth (27.6 per cent) of the budget for the scheme, for current financial year;
(b) the State-wise details of pending funds under wage component; and
(c) the State-wise details of pending funds under material components to the workers?

(a) whether Government maintains the details of those who gave up their Indian citizenship;
(b) if so, the details thereof during the last five years, year-wise; and
(c) the income profile and occupation (in percentage) of such persons during that period?

(a) the details of total number of schools under the Union Government, State-wise;
(b) the total number of these schools which are presently functioning in temporary accommodation, State-wise;
(c) the details of the total sanctioned, filled and vacant teaching positions in these schools, year-wise; and
(d) the details of the total sanctioned, filled and vacant non-teaching staffs in these schools, year-wise?

(a) whether Government maintains data of production and consumption of fertilizers in the country;
(b) if so, the details of existing production and consumption of fertilizers in the country, fertilizer-wise; and
(c) the details, in percentage of total stock exported to other countries, fertilizer-wise?

(a) the number of airports under Public Private Partnership (PPP), the entities operating them and the details thereof;
(b) the passenger volume and the facilities provided by these airports for passengers, airport-wise; and
(c) the revenue generated by these airports after coming under PPP, airport-wise and year-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken any step to strengthen the security arrangements along the Darjeeling Himalayan Railway (DHR) route, which is a UNESCO World Heritage Site;
(b) whether Government has received any proposals for deployment of Railway Protection Force (RPF) or coordination with local police for ensuring passenger and heritage security; and
(c) the number of cases where compassionate appointments have been provided to the dependents of Darjeeling Himalayan Railway (DHR) employees during the last five years?

(a) the number of sanctioned posts, and the number of vacancies, including reserved posts across categories in the Ministry;
(b) the number of vacancies in the Ministry and its Departments, including reserved posts since 2020, year-wise and category-wise ; and
(c) the number of contractual employees hired since 2020, year-wise and category-wise?

(a) the year-wise details of funds allocated and utilised for pollution control during the last five years;
(b) the year-wise details of number of pollution control projects approved, under implementation and completed during those years; and
(c) the reasons behind under-utilisation of funds?

(a) category-wise details of vacancies in each Central University as on 1 November, 2025;
(b) the number of SC, ST, OBC and EWS positions vacant across all Central Universities as of 1 November, 2025;
(c) the number of SC, ST, OBC and EWS candidates rejected on the grounds of ‘not found suitable’ during the last five years and the details thereof; and
(d) whether there is any common recruitment process in the Central Universities, if not, whether Government plans to bring any common recruitment process and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government maintains data on the total number of hospital beds available in the country;
(b) if so, the details thereof, category-wise and the number of hospital beds currently available per 1000 people;
(c) the number of these hospital beds that are owned and managed by Government hospitals; and
(d) the details of Government-owned hospital beds, with a distinction between those managed by State Government and Union Government, State/UT-wise?

(a) whether Government has any data on the homeless people in the country;
(b) if so, the total number of Urban and Rural homeless people, gender-wise, age-wise, as of 31st October 2025; and
(c) the year-wise details of urban slums demolished during the last five years?

(a) whether India has any existing agreements or dialogues with Bhutan regarding flood control or water discharge management of Bhutan-origin rivers;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, whether Government proposes to initiate talks with Bhutan for joint flood mitigation measures?

(a) whether tea garden workers are covered under Central Government welfare schemes such as Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) or Jal Jeevan Mission;
(b) if so, the number of beneficiaries in tea garden areas, particularly in North Bengal; and
(c) whether Government is considering a special welfare package exclusively for tea garden workers?

(a) whether Government is aware that Gorkhas residing outside the Gorkhaland Territorial Administration (GTA) area, especially in districts like Alipurduar, Jalpaiguri, Terai and Dooars, face discrimination or are often overlooked in the recruitment process of the Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs); 
(b) whether Government proposes to give equal recognition and status to all Indian Gorkhas irrespective of their location, whether inside or outside the GTA area, in matters related to recruitment, benefits and representation in CAPFs; and
(c) if so, the steps being taken by Government to ensure this, and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has issued any clarification on social media rumours regarding a ban on paracetamol and other common medicines;
(b) the steps taken to monitor and control price inflation in over-the-counter (OTC) drugs; and
(c) the efforts to ensure uninterrupted supply of essential medicines in rural primary health centers (PHCs) and Government hospitals?

(a) whether there is any proposal to develop Hasimara Airport (West Bengal) for civilian air traffic under UDAN or other schemes;
(b) if so, the details thereof and current status of the proposal; and
(c) the expected timeline for making the airport operational for civil use?

(a) the number of pending wage payments under Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) across different States as of June 2025;
(b) the total unpaid dues for West Bengal; and
(c) the reasons for delay in fund release despite completed work entries on MIS?

(a) whether Central Government has provided or proposes to provide any special package for the social welfare and upliftment of tea garden workers, particularly in West Bengal;
(b) if so, the details of such packages including amount sanctioned, components and implementing agencies; and
(c) the steps taken to ensure that the benefits of such packages reach the tea garden workers directly?

(a) the status of implementation of the ‘Project Elephant’ schemes in West Bengal;
(b) the number of human–elephant conflict incidents recorded in 2024-25 and the compensation paid; and
(c) the steps being taken to fund community-based mitigation and habitat restoration programmes?

(a) the stock levels of essential medicines—including paracetamol and critical antibiotics—held at Central and State warehouses;
(b) the readiness of the National Health Mission to respond to monsoon-related disease outbreaks; and
(c) the inter-ministerial coordination steps for ramping up surveillance and rapid response teams?

(a) whether Government is aware of recurring floods in North Bengal caused by rivers originating from Bhutan;
(b) if so, the details of steps taken by the Central Government to mitigate flood damages in these areas; and
(c) whether any coordination has been undertaken with the Royal Government of Bhutan in this regard?

(a) the progress on the New Maynaguri–Madarihat–Hasimara line project;
(b) the amount of funds allocated in 2024–25 for gauge conversion and station upgrades in North Bengal; and
(c) the expected commissioning date for enhanced passenger and freight services?

(a) the total number of handloom and powerloom weavers registered under national textile schemes in West Bengal;
(b) the financial assistance provided to cooperatives or SHGs in 2024–25; and
(c) the details of cluster development or textile park projects approved for West Bengal?

(a) the number of schools across the country that have been provided training and resources to identify and support students with dyslexia;
(b) the quantum of funds released under the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) for learning-disability remediation in 2024–25; and
(c) plans to roll out standardized assessment tools and teacher-training modules nationally?

(a) whether there is any plan or projects under consideration to upgrade New Jalpaiguri (NJP) into a new Railway Division;
(b) if so, the details thereof including timeline and budget allocation; and
(c) the step taken so far by the Ministry to implement this project?

(a) the numbers of deaths caused due to Human- wildlife conflict, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the manner in which Government plans to compensate victims;
(c) whether Government has any plans to reduce such incidents; and
(d) if so, the details there of?

(a) by when the 11 Left out Gorkhas communities will be granted "Tribal Status"; 
(b) the current status of the proposal for granting ST status to these communities;
(c) the timeline that has been set for the implementation of this decision; and
(d) if not, the reasons thereof?

(a) whether Government has proposed to establish a 200- bed Central Government Hospital in Railway premises at Alipurduar Junction;
(b) if so, the details thereof with current status; and
(c) the total fund allocated for the construction and development of the hospital and utilized so far?

(a) the number of children in Care Homes and shelter homes in the country;
(b) the number of these children have been identified to have special needs;
(c) the number of children who have been adopted in the last five years, year-wise; and
(d) the number of these adopted children who have special needs?

(a) whether Government has any plan or project to set up an All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) in North Bengal;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the proposed location, budget allocation, and timeline for implementation; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to address the healthcare needs of the region through this initiative?

(a) whether Government is aware of the high cost of air tickets on certain routes across the country;
(b) if so, the reasons for the high airfare and the steps taken to regulate and make air travel affordable for passengers; and
(c) whether any measures are being implemented to increase competition and improve connectivity to reduce airfares, particularly on underserved routes?

(a) whether Government has any strategy to extend social welfare protection to tea and cinchona workers;
(b) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government is aware to significant gap in health insurance coverage among tea and cinchona workers; and
(d) if so, the steps Government has taken to bridge this gap and improve insurance coverage for tea and cinchona workers?

(a) the unemployment rate in the age group 18-30 years old in the last five years, urban and rural separately;
(b) the number of unemployed females in the country; and
(c) number of people among the unemployed population who have a graduate or post graduate degree?

(a) whether it is a fact that the PM internship scheme implementation has not been initiated, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of people who have secured internship opportunity under the scheme, the details thereof, State-wise; 
(c) the criteria for selecting companies under the scheme; and 
(d) the number of districts that have less than 10 internship opportunities listed?

(a) whether the AYUSH industry has witnessed significant growth in recent years and contributed significantly to the economy;
(b) if so, the details thereof, for the last five years; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to promote the AYUSH sector, including research, standardization, and global outreach?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has reduced funds towards pre metric scholarship scheme from ? 1199 crores in 2019-20 to just 326 crores in 2024-25, if so, the details thereof and if not, reasons therefor; 
(b) whether it is a fact that the number of scholarships sanctioned under the Pre-Matric Scholarship Scheme from 2018-19 to 2022-23 has been reduced for West Bengal, if so, the details thereof; 
(c) the number of scholarships sanctioned under the Pre-Matric Scholarship Scheme during last three years, State-wise; and
(d) the number of scholarships sanctioned under the Post-Matric Scholarship Scheme during the last three years, State-wise?
