(a) whether Government has any specific plans or projects to develop the North Eastern Region (NER) of the country;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the sectors identified for development, budget allocation and timelines for implementation; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to ensure sustainable development and improve connectivity, infrastructure and employment opportunities in the region?

(a) the number of highway projects sanctioned for West Bengal and its total length;
(b) the progress of ongoing highway projects in the State and its role in shaping the lives of citizen; and
(c) the impact of these projects on the growth of the State?

(a) the details of MoUs signed with different countries for capacity building of civil servants;
(b) the total number of civil servants that are to be trained till 2029; and
(c) the role of capacity building programs in improving service delivery and promoting innovation in governance?

(a) total number of projects sanction under the Brahmaputra Board in recent five years;
(b) the details of budget allocation and expenditure incurred project-wise;
(c) whether there are any plans or projects to form a board similar to the Brahmaputra Board to address flood control and management in North Bengal (West Bengal); and
(d) the specific measures being taken to mitigate the recurring flood situation and ensure the safety and welfare of the affected communities?

(a) the total number of deaths caused due to noncommunicable diseases in the country, year-wise;
(b) the details of measures Government has taken to create awareness and reduce the burden of chronic diseases in the country; and
(c) the manner in which Government plans to provide affordable and robust healthcare services in the country, given that the out-of-pocket expenditure on health is still very high?

(a) year-on-year growth of the AYUSH sector in the last five years;
(b) whether there is a shortage of raw materials, especially due to over reliance on forest produce;
(c) if so, the steps taken by Government to overcome the shortage of raw material; and
(d) whether Government has a concrete strategy to streamline regulatory mechanisms within the AYUSH
sector?

(a) the steps taken by Government to investigate the frequent delays and cancellations of flights in the country;
(b) justification that Government has for high flight tickets prices in the country; and 
(c) whether Government is considering to start civil flights at Hasimara Air Force station in Alipurduar District of West Bengal?

(a) the specific initiatives and programs currently being implemented to uplift the socio-economic conditions of Tribal communities;
(b) the details of schemes launched by Government in recent five years for the welfare of the Tribal communities; and
(c) the measures Government is taking to remove the challenges faced by particular Vulnerable Tribal Group in accessing the welfare schemes?

(a) the number of incidents of examination paper leaks reported in last five years, conducted by central agencies;
(b) the justification Government has for the mismanagement and alleged manipulation of results in the recently conducted NEET exams;
(c) whether any enquiry has been conducted into the working of the National Testing Agency (NTA) due to the rise in complaints of mismanagement, especially after CUET and NEET exams; and
(d) the steps taken to address the psychological and academic impact on students who are affected by examination paper leaks over the last decade?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has issued a Gazette Notification for taking up the running and maintenance of a number of tea gardens in West Bengal;
(b) if so, the present status of the same; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has decided to establish a cross border Rail link between Banarhat in West Bengal and Samtse in Bhutan;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether the concerned State Governments through which the rail will pass through, have been consulted, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether it is a fact that due to the project large section of tea plantation will be destroyed?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government is planning to set up a sports academy in the tea belt of the Dooars region of West Bengal;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and 
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?
